### 3. Additional context (if relevant):
Studies were screened based on the following criteria:
- Index tests: Urea Breath Test (13C/14C), Serology (ELISA, immunoblot, etc.), Stool Antigen Test
- Reference standard: Histopathological examination (H&E, special stains, immunohistochemical stain)
- Population: People suspected of having H. pylori infection

Exclusion reasons included:
- Reviews/meta-analyses/systematic reviews (not primary diagnostic accuracy studies)
- Studies using culture or rapid urease test as sole reference standard
- Studies evaluating other tests (PCR, string test, urine tests) without index tests
- Studies focusing on prevalence, cost-effectiveness, or technical aspects rather than diagnostic accuracy
- Studies comparing index tests to each other without histology reference standard

