  SELECTION CRITERIA APPLIED:                                                                                           
  - Index tests: Urea breath test (13C or 14C), Serology, Stool antigen test                                            
  - Reference standard: Histopathological examination (H&E stain, special stains, or immunohistochemical stain)         
  - Population: People suspected of having H. pylori infection                                                          
  - Study design: Diagnostic accuracy studies                                                                           
                                                                                                                        
  SUMMARY:                                                                                                              
  Total studies screened: {result['n_total']}                                                                           
  Studies included: {result['n_included']}                                                                              
  Studies excluded: {result['n_excluded']}                                                                              
                                                                                                                        
  INCLUDED STUDIES ({result['n_included']}):                                                                            
  These studies evaluated one or more of the specified non-invasive index tests (UBT, serology, stool antigen) against  
  histopathological reference standards in appropriate populations. Key included studies cover:                         
  - Urea breath tests (13C and 14C variants) validated against histology                                                
  - Serological tests (ELISA, whole-blood tests) validated against biopsy/histology                                     
  - Stool antigen tests validated against culture/histology/RUT combinations                                            
                                                                                                                        
  EXCLUDED STUDIES ({result['n_excluded']}):                                                                            
  Exclusion reasons include:                                                                                            
  1. Meta-analyses/Systematic reviews (e.g., studies 410, 411, 421, 459, 461, 470, 487, 499)                            
  2. Treatment trials rather than diagnostic accuracy studies (e.g., 405, 413, 423, 479, 481, 485, 494)                 
  3. Wrong index test - PCR instead of UBT/serology/stool (e.g., 404, 427, 458)                                         
  4. Urine/saliva tests not in protocol-specified index tests (e.g., 420, 426, 442, 455, 469, 480, 482)                 
  5. Rapid urease test only (invasive, not non-invasive) (e.g., 439)                                                    
  6. Prevalence studies without diagnostic accuracy data (e.g., 434, 437, 445, 463, 465)                                
  7. Method development/biomarker studies (e.g., 419, 431, 432, 438, 444, 471, 476)                                     
  8. Wrong reference standard (UBT/culture only, not histology) (e.g., 408, 409, 412, 413, 420, 426, 435, 436, 441,     
  442, 446, 449, 464, 465, 469, 481, 488, 489, 491, 493, 494, 496)                                                      
  9. Quality assessment tool evaluation (484)                                                                           
  10. Histology predictor studies (495)                                                                                 
  11. Wrong organism (Campylobacter) (447)                                                                              
  12. Reviews/commentaries/letters (412, 446, 480, 497)                                                                 
  13. Unclear diagnostic accuracy design or missing key elements                                                        
                                                                                                                        
  CONFIDENCE LEVEL: High for all decisions based on clear title/abstract information."""                                
                                                                                                                        
