  for Helicobacter pylori infection\n\nSELECTION CRITERIA APPLIED:\n- Index tests: Urea breath test (13C or 14C),       
  Serology, Stool antigen test\n- Reference standard: Histopathological examination (H&E stain, special stains, or      
  immunohistochemical stain)\n- Population: People suspected of having H. pylori infection\n- Study design: Diagnostic  
  accuracy studies\n\nSUMMARY:\nTotal studies screened: 100\nStudies included: 34\nStudies excluded: 66\n\nINCLUDED     
  STUDIES (34):\nThese studies evaluated one or more of the specified non-invasive index tests (UBT, serology, stool    
  antigen) against histopathological reference standards in appropriate populations. Key included studies cover:\n-     
  Urea breath tests (13C and 14C variants) validated against histology\n- Serological tests (ELISA, whole-blood tests)  
  validated against biopsy/histology\n- Stool antigen tests validated against culture/histology/RUT                     
  combinations\n\nEXCLUDED STUDIES (66):\nExclusion reasons include:\n1. Meta-analyses/Systematic reviews (e.g.,        
  studies 410, 411, 421, 459, 461, 470, 487, 499)\n2. Treatment trials rather than diagnostic accuracy studies (e.g.,   
  405, 413, 423, 479, 481, 485, 494)\n3. Wrong index test - PCR instead of UBT/serology/stool (e.g., 404, 427,          
  458)\n4. Urine/saliva tests not in protocol-specified index tests (e.g., 420, 426, 442, 455, 469, 480, 482)\n5.       
  Rapid urease test only (invasive, not non-invasive) (e.g., 439)\n6. Prevalence studies without diagnostic accuracy    
  data (e.g., 434, 437, 445, 463, 465)\n7. Method development/biomarker studies (e.g., 419, 431, 432, 438, 444, 471,    
  476)\n8. Wrong reference standard (UBT/culture only, not histology) (e.g., 408, 409, 412, 413, 420, 426, 435, 436,    
  441, 442, 446, 449, 464, 465, 469, 481, 488, 489, 491, 493, 494, 496)\n9. Quality assessment tool evaluation          
  (484)\n10. Histology predictor studies (495)\n11. Wrong organism (Campylobacter) (447)\n12.                           
  Reviews/commentaries/letters (412, 446, 480, 497)\n13. Unclear diagnostic accuracy design or missing key              
  elements\n\nCONFIDENCE LEVEL: High for all decisions based on clear title/abstract information.",                     
