### 3. Additional context (if relevant):
Studies were screened based on the presence of eligible index tests (urea breath test using 13C or 14C, serology, or 
stool antigen test) evaluated against histopathological reference standards (H&E stain, special stains, or 
immunohistochemical stain) in people suspected of having H. pylori infection. 

Exclusion reasons included:
- Secondary research (guidelines, meta-analyses, reviews)
- Studies not evaluating eligible index tests
- Studies lacking histopathological examination as reference standard
- Studies without diagnostic accuracy evaluation (no sensitivity/specificity/comparison metrics)

Included studies evaluate at least one non-invasive test (UBT, serology, or stool antigen) against biopsy-based 
histology in symptomatic or asymptomatic patients suspected of H. pylori infection.
